urname>Hardy</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Murphy</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Pawson</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Screening for PTB domain binding partners and ligand specificity using proteome-derived NPXY peptide arrays</article-title><source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source><year>2006</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>8461</fpage><lpage>8474</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16982700</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Jablonowski</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Raina</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Arce</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Pawson</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Nash</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The human and mouse complement of SH2 domain proteins&#x02014;establishing the boundaries of phosphotyrosine signaling</article-title><source>Mol. Cell</source><year>2006</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>851</fpage><lpage>868</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16793553</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hwang</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Morra</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lillywhite</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Muhandiram</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Gertler</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Terhorst</surname><given-names>C</given-nam